WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.150
Claimant: A supply pipe burst and leaked onto my kitchen floor while I was away, and I found water damage to my personal property when I returned. I reported the loss 44 days after discovering it because I was hospitalized for most of that period; the amount and cause of the damage still need inspection.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:21.400
Adjuster: Were any damaged items discarded or repairs completed before you reported the loss?

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:27.500
Claimant: I don’t know whether any damaged items were discarded or repairs were completed before I reported the loss.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:46.100
Adjuster: Decision: needs_review. The burst-pipe loss is potentially covered, but an adjuster must determine whether the 44-day reporting delay materially prejudiced the investigation. Relevant clauses: HOME-WATER-1, HOME-NOTICE-1, HOME-NOTICE-2. Confidence: 0.99.
